@startuml
title SFA recognition: predicate-labeled transitions over an infinite alphabet

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
  AttributeFontColor #111827
}

[*] --> q0

state "q0\ninitial" as q0 #CCFBF1
state "q1" as q1 #CCFBF1
state "q2\naccepting" as q2 #CCFBF1

q0 --> q1 : [x > 0]
q1 --> q2 : [x < 10]
q1 --> q1 : [x >= 10]
q2 --> [*]

note left of q1
  The edge fires when e ⊨ φ —
  the EBA evaluate(φ, e) oracle
  answers the membership question,
  not a symbol table. One
  predicate-guarded edge stands in
  for every concrete symbol that
  satisfies its guard, so the alphabet
  ℤ stays finite in the machine.
end note

legend bottom
|= Color |= Element |
|<#CCFBF1> | symbolic automaton (SFA) state |
| [φ] | predicate guard on a transition (decided by the EBA) |
endlegend
@enduml
